are not a blanket license for unrelated original project files; include the
module and QEMU additions in the owner's licensing review before distribution.

Dependency source locations, revisions and archive SHA256 values are recorded
in versions.lock. Downloads are made over HTTPS and checked against those
hashes. Release signatures have not been independently verified.

QEMU: GPL version 2 with per-file exceptions and separately licensed components.
Consult COPYING and LICENSE in the pinned release. Its dtc subproject has its
own GPL/BSD licensing. QEMU's bundled Python wheels retain their own licenses.

Buildroot: GPL version 2. Its generated Linux system is a collection of
separately licensed components, not a single Buildroot-licensed binary.
Linux and BusyBox include GPL obligations; the Bootlin toolchain includes GCC,
binutils, glibc and associated source/license obligations. Run make legal-info
and inspect artifacts/build/guest/legal-info before redistribution. That output
is supporting material, not an automatic assertion of legal completeness.

Verilator: installed host tool, dual LGPL-3.0/Artistic-2.0 licensing upstream;
consult the installed version's documentation for generated-output terms.

Xilinx libsystemctlm-soc and systemctlm-cosim-demo: reference-only checkouts.
Remote-Port protocol and representative demo sources contain MIT-style grants;
other files and submodules must be reviewed individually before reuse. The
foundation does not copy, compile or link their code, or fetch their submodules.

Avnet board definitions: reference-only, including the historical Ultra96 V1
tag. Preserve source notices; the older snapshot's disclaimer is not treated
as a blanket redistribution grant. No board XML is copied into project sources.

AMD Vivado/Vitis: proprietary installed software. No installation, license file,
firmware or generated bitstream is included in project sources. Tool discovery
does not grant distribution rights or demonstrate hardware compatibility.

The optional H0 hardware packer downloads Avnet's Ultra96 V1 PYNQ 3.0.1 image;
its URL, release revision and locally measured hashes are recorded separately
in fpga/ultra96-v1/boot-image.lock.json. The derived image retains third-party
firmware, Linux, Ubuntu/PYNQ packages and their notices. It is not covered by
the simulation Buildroot legal-info output. No redistribution-completeness
claim is made for the vendor or derived image; inspect its component licenses
and corresponding-source requirements before distributing it.

The mikro hardware candidate retains that vendor boot partition, including
firmware and Linux, but replaces its root filesystem with Buildroot userspace.
It additionally includes Dropbear; inspect the pinned package's license files.
The networking iteration also includes wpa_supplicant, iw/libnl, OpenSSL/curl,
CA certificate data and e2fsprogs dependencies. Its copied vendor Wi-Fi modules,
firmware and regulatory database retain their separate obligations; the image
includes the vendor linux-firmware copyright file under
/usr/share/licenses/vendor-wifi/copyright. Images optionally containing private
AP credentials must not be published regardless of dependency licensing.
The original axi-mikro-display package records its license as UNKNOWN, pending
the owner's decision. Simulation legal-info does not cover this separate build.
For its userspace inventory, invoke the pinned Buildroot make with the same
BR2_EXTERNAL and O=artifacts/build/ultra96-mikro settings and target legal-info.
The optional PL profile instead uses O=artifacts/build/ultra96-mikro-pl and adds
CPython/libffi plus the original loader, common driver/native applications and
Vivado-generated PL payload. Review that profile's legal-info and the existing
FPGA/vendor obligations separately; the default profile's inventory is not its
complete inventory.
Review that output together with the retained vendor components; no complete
